# dsebd_ca_bundle.crt — CA bundle used ONLY for requests to dsebd.org
# (app/services/market.py). See that module's "TLS" docstring section
# for the full reasoning; the short version:
#
# dsebd.org serves an INCOMPLETE certificate chain. It sends its leaf
# (CN=*.dsebd.org) and the Sectigo ROOT, but omits the intermediate that
# actually signs the leaf — so no client can build a path and both curl
# and requests fail with "unable to get local issuer certificate".
#
# This file supplies the missing link. It is a complete, self-sufficient
# trust path for that one host and NOTHING is disabled: verification is
# still full X.509 path validation (signatures, validity dates,
# hostname), it simply terminates at the genuine Sectigo root below
# instead of at the system store.
#
#   leaf CN=*.dsebd.org
#     └─ signed by → Sectigo Public Server Authentication CA DV R36  (cert 1, the one dsebd.org fails to send)
#          └─ signed by → Sectigo Public Server Authentication Root R46  (cert 2, self-signed public root)
#
# Provenance — both certs were verified, not merely downloaded:
#   * Cert 1 came from the leaf's own AIA extension,
#     http://crt.sectigo.com/SectigoPublicServerAuthenticationCADVR36.crt,
#     and was then checked with `openssl verify` against cert 2.
#   * Cert 2 was NOT downloaded at all. It was extracted from the
#     `certifi` package already installed in this project — i.e. it is
#     the Mozilla CA program's own copy of that root, byte for byte.
#
# So trusting this file is exactly as strong as trusting certifi for
# this host: the same root, reached through one extra intermediate whose
# signature by that root has been checked.
#
# NAMING — PEM-encoded, but named .crt because .gitignore ignores *.pem
# under "Secrets" and this bundle must be committed. It contains public
# certificates only, no private key. (Debian names its own PEM bundle
# /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt for the same non-reason.)
#
# EXPIRY — this file needs replacing before Mar 21 23:59:59 2036 GMT (cert 1).
# When Sectigo reissues, refetch from the AIA URL above and re-verify.
# If dsebd.org ever fixes its chain, delete this file and drop the
# `verify=` argument in app/services/market.py.

# 1) Intermediate — the certificate dsebd.org omits.
#    subject: C=GB, O=Sectigo Limited, CN=Sectigo Public Server Authentication CA DV R36
#    issuer:  C=GB, O=Sectigo Limited, CN=Sectigo Public Server Authentication Root R46
#    valid:   Mar 22 00:00:00 2021 GMT .. Mar 21 23:59:59 2036 GMT
#    sha256:  8C:54:C3:34:B6:6B:A4:E4:26:77:2A:F4:A3:F9:13:6C:19:A1:AE:C7:29:FD:B2:8C:53:5C:07:A5:A4:EF:22:E0
